## Why `DEMO_DB` matters

The project’s normal `.env` database is `glee_test`, which currently has **no platform users**. The `ops@platform.local` account exists only in `glee_demo`, as confirmed by:

```bash
php bin/platform-admin.php list --db=glee_demo
```

No server was running on ports 8000, 8080, or 8142 at the time of this check, so you’ll need to start it as above.

## Create your own platform account

```bash
php bin/platform-admin.php create --db=glee_demo \
  --email=you@example.com \
  --name="Your Name" \
  --password="at-least-12-chars"

php bin/platform-admin.php list --db=glee_demo
```

For a real deployment, create the account without `--db` against your production-style database and don’t keep the demo credentials.